  "label": "Latino immigrants are mapped as desperate individuals willing to risk everything",
  "description": "The text 'latinos will do anything' is mapped onto the visual of people climbing the border fence, implying that the visual action (climbing) represents the textual claim (willingness to do anything). This mapping uses the visual of border crossing to symbolize desperation or extreme determination to enter 'Trump's America', as stated in the text. The visual material (people climbing the fence) is analogically mapped to the textual claim about Latinos' supposed behavior.",
